UID:jt26-d2-6@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T174614Z
DTSTART:20261211T093000Z
DTEND:20261211T113000Z
SUMMARY:Yakiniku in Shibuya
DESCRIPTION:Grill-it-yourself wagyu. All-you-can-eat courses are good valu
 e for three hungry people.\n≈ ¥5\,000–9\,000\nDay 2: Market\, digita
 l art\, Shibuya from above
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-7@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T174614Z
DTSTART:20261211T113000Z
DTEND:20261211T143000Z
SUMMARY:Friday night out
LOCATION:Golden Gai
DESCRIPTION:Nonbei Yokochō (tiny bars by Shibuya Station)\, then stay in 
 Shibuya or JR back (7 min) to Golden Gai: about 200 six-seat bars. Most c
 harge a cover.\ncover ≈ ¥500–1\,000 · drinks ≈ ¥800–1\,200\nDa
 y 2: Market\, digital art\, Shibuya from above
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-8@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T174614Z
DTSTART:20261211T151500Z
DTEND:20261211T164500Z
SUMMARY:Last trains
DESCRIPTION:Last trains leave around 00:15–00:45. After that: taxi (Shib
 uya → Shinjuku ≈ ¥2\,500–3\,500 total) or karaoke until the first 
 train at 05:00. Golden Gai is a 5-min walk from the hotel.\nDay 2: Market
 \, digital art\, Shibuya from above
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Last trains leave in about 30 min
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
